Such application shall be made on a form to be approved by the county administrator/clerk, which form shall require:
(1) The name of the landowner and, if applicable, the person or company performing the construction;
(2) The E-911 address of the structure to be built or a statement indicating why such E-911 address is not necessary;
(3) The square footage of any structures to be built;
(4) The intended purpose of such structures;
(5) The estimated time needed to complete the development;
(6) If known, whether the development activity will occur in any part of a floodplain;
(7) The distance from the development activity to the nearest river or stream;
(8) The tax assessor's parcel ID of the property on which the development activity will occur;
(9) Whether the development will require the construction of any driveways connecting to a county-owned or -maintained road;
(10) Documents showing approval from the health department for any septic tanks or drainage fields that will be placed on the property;
(11) In the case of a mobile home or RV park, a survey, plat, or map of the property showing the proposed number of spaces; the proposed layout of all water and sewerage facilities and structures; and all roads, gutters, drainage systems, and sidewalks intended to be built;
(12) In the case of a residential or commercial subdivision, a survey, plat, or map of the property showing the proposed lots, proposed roads and drainage systems, and any other proposed structures to be built on the property by the developer.
